WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:43.120
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:15.830 --> 02:18.160
Kurosaki Hisoka, 16-years-old.

02:18.270 --> 02:22.500
Died after 3 years in a hospital
from a mysterious incurable illness.

02:22.600 --> 02:23.570
Entered into the register.

02:24.310 --> 02:26.210
"The cause of death
is listed as illness, but"

02:26.310 --> 02:29.470
"there is a possibility
that the victim was murdered."

02:29.580 --> 02:34.070
"But due to lack of evidence,
further investigation was not possible."

02:39.110 --> 02:41.510
Hello? Secret Documents Room...

02:41.860 --> 02:44.350
Oh, Boss?

02:44.460 --> 02:47.220
What?! Hisoka-san was kidnapped?!

02:47.040 --> 02:52.040
Episode 3: Nagasaki Arc, Part 3

02:57.840 --> 03:01.140
Where on earth is that doctor?!

03:02.310 --> 03:03.300
Doctor?

03:06.510 --> 03:07.780
Y-You're...!

03:21.060 --> 03:22.890
Wh-Who are you?!

03:23.500 --> 03:24.330
Y-You...!

03:24.730 --> 03:26.500
I want you to tell me

03:26.600 --> 03:29.090
everything that you know.

03:29.300 --> 03:30.240
I-I don't know anything...

03:30.340 --> 03:32.070
Who is the one you dealt with,

03:32.170 --> 03:36.740
who brought Maria Wong back to life
and has been controlling her?

03:36.840 --> 03:39.640
I-I don't know!
I don't know anything!

03:42.450 --> 03:44.440
I don't have much time.

03:44.650 --> 03:46.090
I can't tell you!

03:46.190 --> 03:48.550
If I tell you, I'll be killed myself!

03:49.760 --> 03:51.050
Dr. Muraki, right?

04:14.950 --> 04:17.780
A rather dangerous toy for a kid.

04:21.160 --> 04:24.060
That wire is a special
netherworld amulet

04:24.160 --> 04:28.690
made from women's hair.

04:28.800 --> 04:30.290
What are you going to do to me?

04:43.280 --> 04:45.010
I'm not going to kill you.

04:45.110 --> 04:48.710
You're the bait that's going
to lure him my way, after all.

04:48.950 --> 04:50.310
Tsuzuki?

04:53.150 --> 04:55.750
<i>What is it?
This sense of darkness I'm getting?</i>

04:55.860 --> 04:59.050
<i>This spirit filled up with sinister intent.</i>

04:59.160 --> 05:01.220
<i>Why is he so sick?</i>

05:01.560 --> 05:03.550
But you really surprised me.

05:03.660 --> 05:06.430
I never thought I'd run into you again.

05:07.100 --> 05:08.860
Have you forgotten?

05:09.100 --> 05:12.730
The sensuous meeting we
had three years ago?

05:13.310 --> 05:14.670
What are you talking about?

05:14.910 --> 05:17.940
Maybe it's time I made you remember.

05:19.850 --> 05:21.470
S-Stop!

05:33.330 --> 05:34.820
Muraki...

05:35.530 --> 05:37.900
What's your objective?

05:40.470 --> 05:42.060
Tsuzuki-san...

05:43.940 --> 05:45.530
I'm sorry.

05:45.870 --> 05:47.930
It was because I was careless.

05:48.210 --> 05:49.770
Tsuzuki-san...

06:01.320 --> 06:02.690
Muraki?

06:11.300 --> 06:12.630
All right.

06:14.030 --> 06:15.630
I'm going to go see Muraki.

06:15.740 --> 06:18.730
You mustn't!
It surely must be a trap!

06:18.840 --> 06:20.770
I don't care if it's a trap

06:20.880 --> 06:23.110
if it means saving Hisoka.

06:23.210 --> 06:24.300
But...

06:27.250 --> 06:29.180
I'll use the spell for giving chase.

06:29.280 --> 06:31.880
It might help determine
Hisoka's whereabouts.

06:37.930 --> 06:39.760
<i>I'm waiting for you.</i>

06:39.960 --> 06:43.260
<i>At the place where we first met.</i>

06:58.410 --> 07:00.570
My prayers have come true.

07:09.820 --> 07:13.660
Tsuzuki-san, I was praying back then

07:14.500 --> 07:16.260
that I'd be able to meet you again.

07:16.860 --> 07:18.130
Where's Hisoka?

07:24.810 --> 07:26.670
Let's go.

07:32.550 --> 07:35.850
Nagasaki certainly has a lot of hills.

07:41.060 --> 07:42.680
Tired out already?

07:56.200 --> 08:00.140
The Christians, who suffered
religious persecution

08:01.080 --> 08:03.980
used Buddha figures on necklaces
to symbolize crucifixes

08:04.080 --> 08:06.100
imbuing it with
the teachings of Christ.

08:08.550 --> 08:12.880
They had to hide their own existence
because of the persecution.

08:13.690 --> 08:15.880
They had to kill their true selves

08:16.360 --> 08:19.690
in order to love others
and keep their faith in God.

08:20.060 --> 08:22.790
I can't imagine what thoughts
were in their minds.

08:22.930 --> 08:25.130
What do you think, Tsuzuki-san?

08:34.270 --> 08:35.470
How beautiful.

08:35.580 --> 08:40.210
Your piercing eyes look like amethyst.

08:40.310 --> 08:41.610
What're you trying to say?

08:41.720 --> 08:43.740
Well, let's go.

08:59.800 --> 09:01.430
Where's Hisoka?

09:02.170 --> 09:04.690
A broken doll can be repaired.

09:04.810 --> 09:07.540
In that sense,
humans have a weakness.

09:07.780 --> 09:11.010
Although modern medicine
continues to advance...

09:11.110 --> 09:15.550
As technology advances,
new illnesses are found...

09:16.750 --> 09:19.280
It's just a vicious circle.

09:19.390 --> 09:21.880
Immortality is a long way away.

09:23.290 --> 09:26.020
The little Jumeau girl...

09:26.130 --> 09:27.790
or the Blu.

09:27.900 --> 09:30.800
Which do you prefer, Tsuzuki-san?

09:35.640 --> 09:37.300
Hisoka...

09:47.380 --> 09:50.010
How many sugars, Tsuzuki-san?

09:52.590 --> 09:55.610
I believe you have a sweet tooth, Tsuzuki-san?

09:56.520 --> 09:59.420
When are we going to see Hisoka?

10:00.090 --> 10:02.430
This place is famous
for its Bavarian Cream.

10:02.530 --> 10:04.190
Cut the crap!

10:08.040 --> 10:10.370
You look wonderful
even when you're angry.

10:10.470 --> 10:11.400
Are you enjoying this?

10:11.510 --> 10:12.340
Yes.

10:12.440 --> 10:13.930
I certainly am.

10:14.040 --> 10:16.370
I enjoy sitting with you like this.

10:19.450 --> 10:22.240
Muraki, what are you trying
to accomplish?

10:22.350 --> 10:26.220
If I caused a major incident,
the Ju-Oh-Cho would act.

10:26.420 --> 10:28.850
It was all so that I could meet you.

10:28.960 --> 10:32.260
I'm your objective?
Then why don't you release Hisoka?!

10:34.930 --> 10:36.900
The kid is fine.

10:37.000 --> 10:39.990
I know quite a lot about that boy.

10:40.100 --> 10:41.590
As to the reason why...

10:41.700 --> 10:45.070
Well, it's because I was the one
who killed that boy.

10:45.170 --> 10:46.470
What?!

10:47.350 --> 10:51.980
Yami no Matsuei

11:01.120 --> 11:02.710
<i>That's right.</i>

11:02.820 --> 11:06.590
<i>That night, I wasn't able
to sleep for some reason.</i>

11:07.190 --> 11:09.030
<i>The night wind blew.</i>

11:22.940 --> 11:24.810
<i>That's right. He was the one...</i>

11:26.250 --> 11:27.770
<i>who killed me.</i>

11:28.780 --> 11:31.750
The boy saw something
he wasn't supposed to.

11:31.850 --> 11:34.290
The face of a brutal murderer.

11:38.660 --> 11:40.680
I could've just killed him there,

11:40.790 --> 11:43.160
and made it look like
the work of a serial killer.

11:43.260 --> 11:46.960
But to simply kill him would
be such a waste, I thought.

11:47.940 --> 11:51.430
A brutal death wouldn't have
suited such a beautiful boy.

11:51.840 --> 11:54.810
I wrestled him to the ground
and took his clothes off

11:55.080 --> 11:57.770
and I cast a haunting spell unto him.

11:59.280 --> 12:02.550
Instead of killing him there,
I took away his memory of that night.

12:03.250 --> 12:07.080
He was gently seduced toward
death under my spell.

12:07.720 --> 12:08.690
That's enough!

12:08.790 --> 12:11.050
I don't want to hear anymore!

12:12.630 --> 12:14.650
I'm the one you want, right?

12:14.760 --> 12:16.730
This should settle it then!

12:16.830 --> 12:20.790
Yes. That was my intention,
but I've changed my mind.

12:21.800 --> 12:23.460
You'll have to wait until later for the reward.

12:23.570 --> 12:24.730
What?!

12:26.110 --> 12:31.010
You've been with me, but you've
only been thinking about that boy.

12:31.110 --> 12:33.410
You're the one that's at fault.

12:44.530 --> 12:46.400
This is where Hisoka-san is...

12:48.960 --> 12:52.870
You lose your composure
when it comes to the boy.

12:52.970 --> 12:56.230
I suppose at least that much
can be forgiven.

12:58.670 --> 13:00.610
Even an immortal Shinigami like him,
with that much blood loss...

13:00.710 --> 13:05.010
I doubt he'll last much longer.

13:05.110 --> 13:06.340
Muraki...!

13:10.280 --> 13:12.010
A messenger...

13:12.420 --> 13:13.910
Well, I'll see you later.

13:20.960 --> 13:23.760
<i>To think this is how I meet my end...</i>

13:24.870 --> 13:28.200
<i>Why do I keep thinking about
him at a time like this?</i>

13:31.940 --> 13:34.310
<i>He sure was a fussy kind of guy.</i>

13:34.410 --> 13:36.880
<i>I wonder what he's doing now.</i>

13:37.880 --> 13:39.710
Hisoka!

13:39.810 --> 13:41.640
Hisoka!

13:44.000 --> 13:45.220
Hisoka-san!

13:45.320 --> 13:46.720
Tsuzuki...!

13:48.090 --> 13:50.060
You're alright now!

13:51.630 --> 13:52.920
Hisoka?

13:53.030 --> 13:54.390
You idiot!

13:55.600 --> 13:57.390
Why did you come and rescue me?!

13:57.500 --> 13:59.690
This is a trap!

14:00.230 --> 14:03.570
I can't abandon you
just because of that.

14:04.710 --> 14:06.400
Tsuzuki...

14:13.380 --> 14:15.210
Pesky little boy, isn't he?

14:15.320 --> 14:17.680
Not only do you distract
Tsuzuki-san from me

14:17.790 --> 14:20.780
but you interfere with my plan!

14:20.890 --> 14:23.410
Plan? Cut it out!

14:23.520 --> 14:28.120
You make Maria suffer, and sacrifice
innocents, and even Hisoka...

14:28.960 --> 14:31.590
We're not tools
that you can use at will!

14:32.000 --> 14:35.060
Muraki, you're one I'll never forgive!

14:39.610 --> 14:42.800
That's the top Shinigami
in the Ju-Oh-Cho for you.

14:42.910 --> 14:47.350
If you won't do as I say,
I'll have to force you into submission.

14:49.580 --> 14:51.810
Do you remember, Tsuzuki-san?

14:52.050 --> 14:54.680
It was because of them
that that child collapsed.

14:54.790 --> 14:56.480
You bastard!

15:06.100 --> 15:08.070
Hisoka-san, hang in there!

15:12.840 --> 15:13.810
A shield...?!

15:13.910 --> 15:16.930
Tsuzuki-san said that you should hold this.

15:22.320 --> 15:24.150
Impressive.

15:24.620 --> 15:27.210
Not a worthy opponent for you.

15:27.320 --> 15:30.260
Now, let's get to the main event.

15:46.410 --> 15:47.460
Damn!

15:58.320 --> 16:02.190
This is as much as he can take!
I've got to set up another shield.

16:02.290 --> 16:05.160
You mustn't!
You've lost too much blood!

16:05.260 --> 16:08.190
Using such crude beasts on me.

16:08.300 --> 16:09.890
I've got a few up my sleeve too!

16:12.230 --> 16:13.220
Hisoka!

16:14.770 --> 16:16.570
How unpleasant.

16:20.740 --> 16:22.040
Hisoka!

16:22.140 --> 16:24.370
What an irritating kid!

16:24.480 --> 16:26.670
I'll vanquish you once again!

16:28.180 --> 16:28.940
Stop!

16:29.050 --> 16:31.980
Just look at me, Tsuzuki-san.

16:32.090 --> 16:34.610
And I want you to show only me

16:34.720 --> 16:37.420
the sight of you as you fall apart!

16:41.760 --> 16:43.530
Stop!

16:57.110 --> 16:58.480
Tsuzuki!

17:00.710 --> 17:01.410
Tsuzuki!

17:01.520 --> 17:03.210
Tsuzuki-san!

17:04.420 --> 17:07.220
It's useless.
After taking a direct hit from that

17:07.320 --> 17:10.550
he won't be able to move
even if he is a Shinigami.

17:11.530 --> 17:14.490
All right, kid.
Get out of the way!

17:14.730 --> 17:16.490
He belongs to me.

17:20.630 --> 17:22.070
<i>C-Can you hear me?</i>

17:22.170 --> 17:25.900
<i>I know this is going to be hard on you,
but you'll have to bear it.</i>

17:26.270 --> 17:27.500
<i>I-I'm fine!</i>

17:27.880 --> 17:29.930
<i>I want to borrow your strength.</i>

17:30.040 --> 17:32.570
<i>A-All right. What should I do?</i>

17:33.050 --> 17:35.780
<i>Let me synchronize with you.</i>

17:35.880 --> 17:37.580
<i>I'll use your body and cast a spell.</i>

17:37.680 --> 17:39.910
<i>But what'll happen to you?</i>

17:40.020 --> 17:43.850
<i>Please, Hisoka. At this rate,
we're both finished.</i>

17:44.730 --> 17:46.020
<i>All right.</i>

17:49.560 --> 17:51.790
A beautiful display of friendship.

17:51.900 --> 17:54.030
But it offends me.

17:57.570 --> 17:58.270
Wha...?!

18:05.180 --> 18:07.980
Don't tell me they've combined their powers!

18:08.080 --> 18:10.050
Where did they get that power?!

18:10.750 --> 18:12.550
I bow to thee and beseech you.

18:12.750 --> 18:15.280
The Twelve Gods that protect me.

18:15.390 --> 18:17.580
Appear before me!

18:17.690 --> 18:19.420
Come out! Suzaku!

18:33.940 --> 18:35.340
Suzaku!

18:35.780 --> 18:36.540
Explode!

18:36.640 --> 18:38.580
How impertinent!

18:51.760 --> 18:53.190
Awesome!

18:53.290 --> 18:55.960
Now I want you even more...

18:56.060 --> 18:57.220
Tsuzuki-san.

18:57.330 --> 18:58.530
Muraki...

18:59.170 --> 19:01.530
I'm sure I'll see you again.

19:09.380 --> 19:11.900
Tsuzuki-san... Hisoka-san...

19:21.120 --> 19:22.950
Thank goodness!

19:39.710 --> 19:40.670
Tsuzuki...

19:40.910 --> 19:43.930
You're recovering, aren't you?
Don't push it.

19:44.040 --> 19:45.010
That goes for you too.

19:48.150 --> 19:51.950
Do you know why I became
a Shinigami?

19:53.290 --> 19:56.190
It was to find the one
who killed me.

19:56.790 --> 19:58.880
I knew that there was
nothing I'd be able to do

19:58.990 --> 20:02.090
if I were to find him at this stage.

20:02.200 --> 20:05.960
But I wanted to know the truth.

20:06.500 --> 20:09.730
Have you resolved your issues
by confronting Muraki?

20:09.840 --> 20:11.200
I don't know.

20:11.300 --> 20:16.140
The darkness of his spirit was so deep.
I couldn't figure it out.

20:17.180 --> 20:20.540
So, what are you planning
on doing now?

20:20.650 --> 20:21.410
Who knows.

20:21.520 --> 20:26.510
If you don't want to partner with me,
we can go our separate ways.

20:26.690 --> 20:27.880
I suppose.

20:27.990 --> 20:31.220
You are quite a handful, after all.

20:31.320 --> 20:34.890
Besides, you're a kid, and you'll
never listen to my advice.

20:36.600 --> 20:39.690
Or so I thought, but I changed my mind.

20:40.530 --> 20:42.900
Looking forward
to working together, Hisoka.

20:43.740 --> 20:45.200
Tsuzuki...

20:45.410 --> 20:49.240
Who knows. That creep
might come after you again.

20:49.340 --> 20:52.370
I'd be there to save you
if that were to happen.

20:53.050 --> 20:56.410
Why do you care so much about a stranger?

20:56.520 --> 21:01.180
When I was about to be killed,
it was like you took it personally.

21:01.290 --> 21:03.520
Why are you doing this for me?!

21:05.090 --> 21:07.790
Why? I'm just...
I'm just a...

21:10.660 --> 21:12.000
Because you're my partner.

21:15.800 --> 21:17.360
Seems foolish.

21:18.770 --> 21:20.360
Let's get something to eat.

21:20.470 --> 21:22.940
Let's celebrate our new partnership.

21:23.040 --> 21:25.710
Hey! Don't just decide on your own!

21:25.810 --> 21:27.300
Hey, what do you want eat?

21:27.410 --> 21:29.880
First of all,
I don't think we can afford it.

21:29.980 --> 21:31.950
We had Chinese the other day.

21:32.050 --> 21:35.180
Japanese? Italian?
How about super-spicy Thai food?

21:35.290 --> 21:38.190
I'm not going to take the fall
if Tatsumi-san gets pissed off.

21:39.960 --> 21:42.960
Next Episode

21:44.030 --> 21:47.090
Violin prodigy, Hiji Minase.

21:47.500 --> 21:49.400
Death is courting him.

21:49.770 --> 21:52.700
What is the terrible secret
hidden in the Devil's music?

21:52.810 --> 21:55.830
Tsuzuki-san, we have to hurry
to Kumamoto right away!

21:55.940 --> 21:58.340
All right! We'll have to eat
some horse sashimi first!

21:58.450 --> 22:00.280
Food again?

22:00.060 --> 22:09.910
Episode 4: Devil's Trill, Part 1

22:00.610 --> 22:05.640
Next time on Yami no Matsuei:
The Devil's Trill, Part 1

22:05.750 --> 22:09.590
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.230 --> 22:21.590
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.700 --> 22:24.630
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.730 --> 22:28.220
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.340 --> 22:30.930
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.040 --> 22:38.270
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.380 --> 22:45.010
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.470 --> 23:04.890
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.410 --> 23:11.340
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.110 --> 23:18.450
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.200 --> 23:24.600
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
